# sm119, the clay-digger by the door (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sm119
revision 2
state ready
dialect southmeadow
accent none
tier standard
written_for cty_briar_sedgebridge
written_by claude
title the clay-digger by the door
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=miner humour=merry
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=warm humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk never_sits_with_a_back_to_the_door
likes mutton_stew draughts festival_bells frosty_mornings
dislikes crowds stale_bread
fears a_secret_spoken_in_the_wrong_room knees_that_quit_before_the_work_does
hopes a_long_life_of_laughing a_winter_with_the_pot_always_full
topics pastimes +0.4 food +0.4 festival +0.3 friends +0.3 work +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=company gossip=teasing refuse=soft tease=merry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# works hard and laughs at it, talks the ears off anyone at the table, always takes the seat facing the door, and knows one story about a big House that will never be told.

words
door = the door | the front door
uncle = an old uncle of mine | my old uncle
oath! = By my muddy elbows | Clay to the knees
saying! = Sit facing the door and you'll never miss a friend | A laugh costs nothing and keeps all winter
seat = the seat facing the door | my chair by the wall
pit = the pit | the clay pit
clay = clay | good grey clay
barrow = the barrow | a barrow of wet clay
pot = a mutton pot | mutton stewed till it falls apart
draughts = a round of draughts | the draughts board
bells = the feast bells | bells on a feast morning
frost = white frost | frost on the ruts
crush = a press of folk | too many folk in one room
stale = stale bread | bread gone hard as a step
knees = my knees | these old knees
tale = that tale | the one I don't tell

any
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : I work all week and still count pennies at the counter, and the shelves never look hungry. Make that add up, #address#. | Prices go up like bread in an oven. My pay sits there like #stale#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The Houses? I could tell you a thing about one of them. I won't; it's #tale#. That's my opinion, and it's a long one.
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : The minute #bells# start I'm off, and I don't come home till my feet give out.
opinion @1 drink for 1 : A cup with friends at the end of a long day. Nothing wrong with that, and plenty right, #oath#.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Every week the purse gets lighter and #work# doesn't. Nobody up the hill seems to notice.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : Bring a stranger in and feed them, I say. Only leave me #seat#.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Come in, come in. Mind, that seat's mine. | #greet#. Don't stand in #door#way; I can't see past you.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=miner] : #greet#. Don't shake my paw, it's all #clay#. | #greet#. Stand back from the edge; #pit# bites.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Up with the birds, are you? So am I, and I'm louder. | #greet#. A #cold# start, and all the better for it.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Pull a stool round; I've #door# in my eye. | #greet#. Late for visiting. I'm glad you did.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are! Sit, sit. Not that side; that's #seat#. | #greet#. I've kept the pot on for you.
line @1 again.open : Back twice before #supper#. I'll be charging rent on that stool soon. | You again. #good.capitalize#, I'd run out of things to tell the wall.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! Look who it is. | #greet#, #address#. Sit where I can see you, you and #door# both.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family|spouses] : #greet#. Took you long enough. Sit. | #greet#. I've saved you a laugh.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Mind my paws; they're filthy. | #greet#. Talk while I work; I can do both.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Off you go; I'll be watching #door#. | #farewell#. Come back when you've a story.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Go careful; the ruts are deep after dark. | Off you go. #farewell#, and sleep sound.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#! Keep laughing. | #farewell#, #address#. Mind how you go.
line @1 react.news : Go on! That's one for the fireside. | #surprise#. Well, there's a thing.
line @1 react.news.new : Never! You've caught me out there, #address#, and that takes doing. | #oath#, that's news to me.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Old news by now. | I'd heard. Somebody shouted it across the lane at #supper#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Somebody's stretching that like wet #clay#. | Show me somebody who saw it, not a rumour off a cart.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's a #bad# thing for anyone. | Oh, that's hard. My heart goes out to them.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#! I'll drink to that with whatever's going. | Well, that's lovely. Somebody ring #bells#.
line @1 answer.how : Muddy and merry, same as ever, #address#. | #good.capitalize#. #knees.capitalize# say otherwise, but nobody asked them.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Up to the elbows in it. Talk while I dig. | Busy as bees, and loving the sound of my own voice.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Keeping out of trouble, or in it? | How are you keeping, #address#? Truly, now.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Come and sit by the fire with me. | Oh, #address#. That's a #bad# business. Sit down.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. I've seen worse mended. | It'll come round. Most things do, given a laugh and a week.
line @1 decline : I'd like to, truly, but I've no coin to spare this week, and that's the honest end of it. | Not this time, #address#. Too many folk in one place for me; go and tell me about it after.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Next time, then. | Fair enough. I'll hold you to the next one.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. You're a treasure. | #thanks#. I'll not forget that.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | Get away with you. It was nothing at all.
line @1 preclose : Listen to me, talking the day out. #excuse#. | #preclose#. #knees.capitalize# want their chair.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. Mind #door#. | Off you go. I've talked your ear thin.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends|family|spouses] : That's a long face for a short day. Who stole your pudding? | Is that the same coat? It's been to more feasts than I have.
line @1 tease.return : #cheek#. | Says the one with porridge on the chin.
line @1 ack : #bc_ha# | #bc_true#. Go on.
line @1 give.advice : Sit where you can see #door#. You'll thank me one day. | Laugh first. Worry after, if there's time.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep to the road, and if you stop, keep a wall at your back. | Bandits about, they say. Sit facing #door# tonight.
rule @pit_lift
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=miner
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Up you come, you heavy lump of #clay#. | Another #barrow#. #oath#, my arms.

rule @door_watch
when concept=bark here.place=tavern|home|hall
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Shift up, would you? I want the wall at my back and #door# in front. | Who's that coming in? Oh. Only the wind.

rule @crowd_wall
when concept=bark here.crowd=busy|crowd
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #crush.capitalize#, elbows everywhere. I'll be by the wall. | I'll wait till #crush# thins, thank you.

rule @bells_out
when concept=bark world.festival=today
does aside
cooldown 12h
say #bells.capitalize#! Somebody find me my good shawl. | There they go. Dancing, whoever's with me.

scene door_seat
when topic=smalltalk|day here.place=tavern|home|hall|chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Shift along, would you? I like #seat#. | I always take the chair facing #door#. Always have. | You're in #seat#. No, stay; I'll stand till you're done.
b : What's wrong with this side? | Why's that? | It's only a chair.
a : Nothing, if you don't mind folk coming up behind you. I do. | So I see who's coming and wave first. I like to be first. | It's only a chair to you. To me it's the one facing #door#.
b : Fair enough. | Handy, that. | Have it, then.
a : #bc_ha# #saying.capitalize#. | And I'm never caught with my mouth full. Mostly. | #thanks#. I'll keep you company from here, and keep an eye on #door#.

scene door_why
when topic=smalltalk|memories pair.band=friends|family|spouses
does confide / react.self / assess
a : #vent#: it isn't really about waving first. I just rest easier knowing who's come in. | #uncle.capitalize# sat with his back to a door once and never heard the end of it. I learned from him. | I tell everyone it's so I see friends first. That's half of it.
b : That's nothing to be ashamed of. | What happened to him? | And the other half?
a : I'm not ashamed. Just careful, and #very# merry with it. | Somebody poured a jug of milk down his collar at a wedding. He was never the same. | The other half stays with me. Have #pot#.

scene house_hint
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : I know a story about one of the big Houses that would curl your whiskers. | There's a thing I saw once, years back, that a House would pay to have forgotten. | Folk think the Houses are all silver and manners. I know better, and that's all I'll say.
b : Go on, then. | What did you see? | That's not all, surely.
a : Not for all the mutton in the town. It stays behind my teeth. | Something. And that's the whole of what you'll get from me. | It is. I like my head where it is. #bc_ha#
b : You're a terrible tease. | Fair enough. | Now I'll wonder all night.
a : I am. It's my one fault. Two, with #draughts#. | #good.capitalize#. #saying.capitalize#. | Wonder away. Wondering's free, #address#.

scene pit_dig
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=miner
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #clay.capitalize# came up lovely today. Grey as a rain cloud and twice as slippery. | Eleven barrows before noon. #oath#, my arms are singing. | Lost a boot in #pit# this morning. It's down there still, making friends.
b[job=miner|laborer] #dig : Good clay's worth the sweat. | Eleven's a fair morning. | We've all left a boot somewhere.
b : Sounds hard going. | Eleven! | A whole boot?
a@dig : It is, and the potters know it, even if they don't say. | It is. I'll be no use to anybody by supper. | Mine's the third this year. #oath#.
a : Hard, but honest, and I laugh at it. #bc_ha# | Eleven, and every one heavier than the last. | The whole boot. I hopped home singing.

scene pit_rain
when topic=weather|work self.job=miner here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# on #clay#. You can't stand straight in #pit# for sliding. | Wet days #pit# turns to soup. I came home grey to the ears.
b : Can't you wait it out? | I'd stay home.
a : Not when we're paid by the barrow. Slide or go hungry, #address#. | I'd love to. The purse won't hear of it.

scene creaky_knees
when topic=health self.age>=45
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : #knees.capitalize# creak like an old cart, and they're louder than I am, which takes doing. | I'm a #very# young wolf with a very old pair of knees.
b : That sounds a trial. | Mine are going too.
a : It is. Still, they've carried me this far, and they can grumble all they like. | Then we'll creak along together, #knees# and yours, and nobody will hear either of us.

scene mutton_pot
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's #pot# on the fire since noon. You can smell it from the lane. | Nothing in the world beats #pot# on a #cold# night. Nothing. | I'd walk a mile for #pot#. I'd walk back for seconds.
b : It does smell good. | Not even cake? | Two miles for stew?
a : Come and have a bowl. Sit wherever you like, but #seat#. | Not even cake. Cake's for after. | Three, if there's bread to mop it.

scene stale_loaf
when topic=food|prices
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Bought a loaf yesterday and it was #stale# by the time I got home. | I'll eat most things. #stale.capitalize# isn't one of them.
b : They keep the old ones for last thing. | Toast it.
a : Then I'll go first thing and fight for a fresh one. #bc_ha# | I did. It still tasted like a doorstep.

scene draughts_game
when topic=pastimes
does invite / accept_invite / tease / tease.return / laugh
a : Fancy #draughts#? I'll even let you have white. | I've got the board out. Sit down and lose to me, #address#.
b : Go on, then. | You'll lose this time.
a : Sit there, then. No, the other chair. I need #door#. | We'll see. I've won forty in a row against everybody on my street.
b : Fussy, aren't you. | Forty? I don't believe it.
a : Particular. Not the same thing, and the difference wins me games. | Forty-one, after this one. #bc_ha#

scene feast_bells
when topic=festival
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : When #bells# go, I'm out #door# before the second peal. | Hear that? #bells.capitalize#. I could dance on a dead knee. | Give me one day of dancing over a month of rest. I've tried both.
b : They do lift you. | Mind the knee. | Which won?
a : They do. Even #knees# join in. | I'll mind it after. Dancing first. | The dancing, by a mile. #bed.capitalize# is still sulking.

scene white_morning
when topic=weather|season here.time=dawn here.season=autumn|winter here.weather=clear
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Look at that. #frost.capitalize# on everything, and the air like a #cold# apple. | A morning like this, I take the long way to work, just to crunch #frost#. | I love a #cold# clear morning. Everything sounds closer.
b : It's lovely, if you're dressed for it. | The long way? In this? | It does.
a : I'm dressed for it. Two shawls and a grin. | The long way. Work isn't going anywhere. | #oath#, I could hear a mouse across the field.

scene too_many
when topic=smalltalk|day here.crowd=busy|crowd
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Too many folk in one place. I can't see #door# for heads. | #crush.capitalize#. I'll stand by the wall, thanks, where I can breathe. | I like folk one at a time. Ten at once, I want my own kitchen.
b : It is a bit much. | Can't blame you. | One at a time is better.
a : A bit much and then some. I'll go round the back. | #bc_ha# I'll be the one in the corner, waving. | It is. You count as one. A #good# one.

scene married_lucky
when topic=family|home self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd not swap my #self.spouse_word# for a House and all its silver. | I married the one who lets me have #seat#. That's love, that is. | Married all these years and I still talk too much at #supper#.
b : That's a lovely thing to say. | Or patience. | You do talk.
a : It's true, so it's easy to say. | Patience, then. Either way, I'm lucky. | I do. And I'll keep at it till the green ground takes me.

scene old_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# and I go back years. I'd trust #self.friend# with my last penny. | If I had one friend left in the world, I'd want it to be #self.friend#.
b : That's a rare thing. | That's a good friend to have.
a : It is. I don't say it enough, #address#. | The best kind. #saying.capitalize#.

scene light_purse
when topic=prices|times self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : I work all week and still count my #money# for bread. Somebody's doing well; it isn't me. | The purse is lighter every week, and the work's no lighter at all.
b : It's hard for a lot of folk. | Nobody up the hill notices.
a : It is. Still, I've a laugh left, and they can't tax that. | They don't. I notice enough for all of them, #oath#.

scene theft_talk
when topic=crime|gossip topic.claim_kind=theft
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd lock my door, if I had a door worth locking. | Folk are saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'm sitting facing #door# tonight, I can tell you.
b : I'd heard something of it. | You always do.
a : Well, now you've heard it twice. Mind your purse. | I do. Tonight I'll mean it, #address#.

scene chapel_singing
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The Bright One hears my thanks on the walk home. It's quieter than chapel, and there's no plate going round. | I go to chapel for the singing. The praying I can do anywhere, #address#.
b : There's sense in that. | The singing's good.
a : Plenty of sense, and no collection. #bc_ha# | It is, when nobody's flat. Mostly I'm the flat one.

scene full_cottage
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our house is #very# full. Somebody's always cooking, somebody's always singing. | I like a house with noise in it. Quiet makes me listen for #door#.
b : Sounds a happy house. | That's the habit again.
a : Happy and crowded, and I'd have it no other way. | It is. I can't help it, #address#. #bc_ha#

scene same_fields
when topic=memories|land here.region=southmeadow self.from=southmeadow self.age>=30
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : I gleaned these same fields when I was a #child#. Now I just walk past them and wave. | I've lived in #here.town# all my days. I know which gate squeaks on every lane.
b : You'd know them better than most. | Every gate?
a : Every furrow. They've known me just as long. | Every one. I could find my way home by the squeaks alone, #oath#.

story first_day_pit [topic=work|memories self.job=miner self.age>=30]
  : My first day at #pit#, I stepped where the ground looked firm and went in up to my middle.
  : The old diggers stood round the edge of #pit# and laughed till they cried, and then they pulled me out.
  ask : Do you know what I did then?
  b : Went home and never came back, I'd guess.
  : Laughed louder than any of them, and went back in with a spade. #saying.capitalize#.

story uncle_milk [topic=memories|family self.age>=25]
  : #uncle.capitalize# sat with his back to #door# at a wedding supper.
  : A pup with a jug of milk came up behind, tripped on the step, and down it went, all of it, inside his collar.
  ask : Can you guess where I've sat ever since?
  b : Facing the door, I'd say. Did he laugh?
  : Not that night. The next year, he told it louder than anyone. And I've faced #door# since.

story the_house_tale [topic=gossip|memories self.age>=40]
  : Years ago I saw a thing at the back door of a big House that I was never meant to see.
  : I've carried it ever since, the way you'd carry a hot coal in a spoon.
  ask : Would you tell a thing like that, if it were yours?
  b : I don't think I would. Will you tell me, though?
  : Not if you poured me cider till dawn. That's why I'm still here to laugh about it.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. Come in, sit down. Not that chair; that one faces #door#, and it's mine. | #greet#. A new face. Pull up a stool and tell me who you are.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#! Sit where I can see you. | #topic.player#! #greet#. Back for more of my talk?
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : #greet#. Late, isn't it? I heard #door# and had to look.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : #greet#. I'll keep my seat and you keep your distance, and we'll get on fine.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=miner] : #clay.capitalize#. I dig it, barrow it and ache from it. #self.trade_words.capitalize#, if you want it proper. | #clay.capitalize#, all day long. The potters get the glory and I get the mud.
dlg @2 resident.job : A bit of everything, and too little #money# for any of it. | #job_busy#
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Ask me again on a feast day. | Nothing worth the breath. I've a story, but it isn't news, and it isn't yours.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : I know one tale worth telling, and I'll not tell it. | #gossip_none#
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind #door# on your way; I'll be watching it. | #farewell#. Come back with a story.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you always sit facing the door? -> door
node door
say So I can see who's coming and wave first. And so nobody pours milk down my collar. An old uncle taught me that, the hard way.
mood pleased
free
choice Milk down your collar? -> door_milk
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node door_milk
say Down his collar, at a wedding supper. He never sat with his back to a door again, and nor have I. Sit where you like, only not there.
choice I'll sit elsewhere. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
